acks is printed +14%, where every other bonus in the entry is a multiple of five; stored as printed (42 + 14 = 56). Speaks two additional languages prints no bonus. The two piloting picks of choice print any except robot vehicles, power armor and ships; the exclusion is in the note. W.P. Heavy Energy Weapon is stored as the catalog row W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons. Gymnastics and General Athletics print no bonus. Related skills: one skill of choice plus one piloting skill at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12 is stored as two picks at each of those levels with the piloting condition in the note. || MONEY: 2D4x100 credits stored (the text layer prints 2D4xlOO); the 2D4x100 credits of tradeable goods and the 750 credit monthly salary are in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: one weapon for each W.P.; bedroll, belt, boots, cloak or cape (often fur) and personal items have no row; the starting vehicle of choice (Tek-12 YY110 Bushbike, Tek-20 YY210 ''Borgbike, Warrior AH-Hoversled, Landflier or any snow mobile or jet sled) has no row. The armor row is this book''s homemade medium armor (50-65 M.D.C.), the nearest to the printed 50-60. The jet pack is this book''s common jet pack row. The silver cross, tinted goggles and lighter use the nearest catalog rows and say so in their notes. || NOT STORED: the proportions of cyborgs among the RMC (the lore says 43% partial and about 12% full conversion; the Cybernetics line says 8% Light Machines, 4% Heavy Machines and another 50% with one to three bionic prosthetics), which the two passages print differently."
